# Operations Workspace — Context Anchor

Anchors platform context for sessions rooted anywhere under the operations
workspace. This file **references**; it never restates.

## How to resolve the paths below

Every path below is relative to **this file's own location** — the
operations-workspace root. Resolve each one from here, never from the session's
working directory. A session that loads this anchor may be rooted at any depth
beneath it, so its working directory is not a usable base: read cwd-relatively
from the operations root, the first entry would resolve to this anchor itself.
Relative to this file, `../` is the workspace root.

## What an operations-rooted session loads

1. `../CLAUDE.md` — workspace charter: universal rules, routing, quality standards
2. `../pmo-platform/core/governance/OPERATIONS.md` — PMO protocols, cross-project rules
3. `_config/SESSION_STATE.md` — session handoff state
4. `_config/CORRECTIONS.md` — platform-wide behavioral redirects
5. `<Project>/PROJECT.md` — active project context
6. `<Project>/CORRECTIONS.md` — project-scoped redirects (absent is normal)
7. `<deploy-root>/.claude/rules/_operations-index.md` — the agent-conduct rules this
   session loads, and the rules it names. Generated by the deploy; absent means the
   rules mirror has not been deployed here

Context files accumulate: this anchor adds to whatever the runtime already
resolved from an ancestor directory, and replaces none of it. The charter's
Session Management section is authoritative on the full session-start sequence,
including surfaces not named here.

## Invariant

Any procedure appearing here in full rather than as a pointer is a shadow SSOT
and must be removed — see
`../pmo-platform/core/disciplines/knowledge-architecture.md`, Memory-corpus
boundary section.
